1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,287
A help page can hold questions and tips that editors add, reorder, and

2
00:00:05,287 --> 00:00:06,923
remove inside the page.

3
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:10,251
The Bag part of the Flows module makes that possible.

4
00:00:10,251 --> 00:00:14,200
We add a Bag to a content type, fill it, and see it on the site.

5
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:22,290
A content part adds one capability to a content type.

6
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:26,489
The Bag part lets a content item hold other content items, of the

7
00:00:26,489 --> 00:00:28,323
content types you choose.

8
00:00:28,323 --> 00:00:31,280
Editors add them from the page's own editor.

9
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:36,433
The items are stored inside the page's own document, so they are saved

10
00:00:36,433 --> 00:00:38,055
and published with it.

11
00:00:38,055 --> 00:00:42,110
Each item is a full content item, with its own parts and fields.

12
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:46,135
The Flows module has a second part, the Flow part.

13
00:00:46,135 --> 00:00:50,053
A Flow part holds widgets, each with an alignment and a size.

14
00:00:50,053 --> 00:00:55,200
A Bag part holds items of the content types you choose and has no layout settings.

15
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,943
The Bag part comes with the Flows feature.

16
00:00:58,943 --> 00:01:01,250
Recipes such as Blog enable it.

17
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:05,240
On any other site, you enable Flows under Tools, Features.

18
00:01:09,475 --> 00:01:14,791
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, we see every content type.

19
00:01:14,791 --> 00:01:19,385
We select Create new type, name it Help Page, and select Create.

20
00:01:19,838 --> 00:01:23,354
The Add Parts page lists the parts a type can use.

21
00:01:23,354 --> 00:01:28,188
We tick Title, so every page has a name, and select Add Selected Parts.

22
00:01:28,666 --> 00:01:33,095
We add the bag as a named part, so the type could hold several bags.

23
00:01:33,095 --> 00:01:36,806
On the Edit Content Type page, we select Add Named Part.

24
00:01:37,262 --> 00:01:40,120
We call the part Help Items and describe it.

25
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:41,891
The Bag part is selected.

26
00:01:41,891 --> 00:01:44,292
Save & Configure opens its settings.

27
00:01:44,774 --> 00:01:49,333
Contained Content Types offers two choices, Content Types and Stereotype.

28
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:53,834
We keep Content Types, and tick Question and Tip, two content types that

29
00:01:53,834 --> 00:01:57,354
already exist on this site and that this bag will hold.

30
00:01:57,807 --> 00:02:01,898
Display Type is the display type the site uses for each item, and

31
00:02:01,898 --> 00:02:03,914
an empty value means Summary.

32
00:02:03,914 --> 00:02:08,927
Collapse Contained Items makes saved items start collapsed when the editor opens.

33
00:02:08,927 --> 00:02:09,907
We tick it.

34
00:02:10,412 --> 00:02:12,305
The editor stays Standard.

35
00:02:12,305 --> 00:02:18,162
Selecting Save stores the settings and returns to the type, which lists Title and Help Items.

36
00:02:22,454 --> 00:02:27,547
Under Content, Content Items, the New button lists the content types we can create.

37
00:02:27,547 --> 00:02:29,034
We choose Help Page.

38
00:02:33,703 --> 00:02:35,929
We type a title, Account Help.

39
00:02:35,929 --> 00:02:38,031
The Help Items bag is empty.

40
00:02:38,031 --> 00:02:42,173
Because it accepts two content types, its button is Add Item.

41
00:02:42,697 --> 00:02:44,610
Add Item lists the two types.

42
00:02:44,610 --> 00:02:45,977
We choose Question.

43
00:02:45,977 --> 00:02:49,694
A card opens with the fields of that content type, a Title and

44
00:02:49,694 --> 00:02:51,717
an Answer, and we fill them in.

45
00:03:01,206 --> 00:03:04,938
Choosing Tip from Add Item appends a second card at the end of

46
00:03:04,938 --> 00:03:07,791
the bag, and we fill in its Title and Details.

47
00:03:07,791 --> 00:03:10,206
The items keep the order of the cards.

48
00:03:15,491 --> 00:03:16,887
We select Publish.

49
00:03:16,887 --> 00:03:20,551
The items are saved and published together with the page.

50
00:03:24,782 --> 00:03:28,806
When we edit the page again, the saved items load collapsed, because of

51
00:03:28,806 --> 00:03:30,269
the setting we ticked.

52
00:03:30,269 --> 00:03:32,202
The arrow on a card expands it.

53
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:35,197
The handle at the left of a card moves it.

54
00:03:35,197 --> 00:03:39,220
We drag the Tip above the Question, and the order of the items changes.

55
00:03:40,156 --> 00:03:44,847
The red trash button removes an item, after asking for confirmation.

56
00:03:44,847 --> 00:03:47,066
We cancel, so the item stays.

57
00:03:49,103 --> 00:03:52,583
Publish saves the reordered items together with the page.

58
00:03:56,788 --> 00:04:01,142
In the Content Items list, View opens the published page in another tab.

59
00:04:01,142 --> 00:04:04,770
Under the title, the site shows the items of the bag in the

60
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:07,058
order of the editor, the Tip first.

61
00:04:11,316 --> 00:04:13,398
The Bag part has a second editor.

62
00:04:13,398 --> 00:04:17,561
In the part's settings, the question What type of editor should be used?

63
00:04:17,561 --> 00:04:19,322
offers Standard and Blocks.

64
00:04:19,322 --> 00:04:22,151
We choose Blocks, and two more settings appear:

65
00:04:22,151 --> 00:04:24,446
Add Button Text and Modal Title Text.

66
00:04:24,904 --> 00:04:31,124
We leave both empty, which keeps the defaults, Add Block and Select Block, and select Save.

67
00:04:31,626 --> 00:04:34,935
In the page editor, the button reads Add Block.

68
00:04:34,935 --> 00:04:38,556
It opens a dialog with a card for each content type.

69
00:04:38,556 --> 00:04:41,926
Selecting Add on a card adds an item to the bag.

70
00:04:43,926 --> 00:04:47,537
The Bag part keeps a group of content items inside a page, and

71
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:50,246
editors manage them in the page's own editor.

72
00:04:50,246 --> 00:04:51,626
Thanks for watching.

